# Godfrey dialog state

When changing Godfrey body animation, idle selection, listening/speaking holds, or presence flow, respect **in-dialog vs out-of-dialog**.

## Meaning

- **Out of dialog:** game start (SeaIdle), or after a farewell AS has started / finished (returning to sea).
- **In dialog:** from engage until farewell begins. A new visitor’s first turn is **webcam presence** (arrival card + Greeting while the card is up, spoken Welcome as soon as it clears / R17), not the microphone. Visitor speech engages only after that Welcome, or if the webcam is off.

API: `UGodfreyPerformanceStateComponent::IsInDialog()` (Engaging + Conversing).

Living tracker: `Docs/GodfreyBehaviourRules.md` (R7, R8, R9, R13, R14, R15, R17, R20, R23).

## Animation rules

- **In dialog:** after an optional first Greeting* hold (R15), attentive listening-pool idles only (`ListeningAttentive` / `Curious` / `Concerned` / `Nodding`) **while Speak is green**. When the lantern is Wait (visitor finished, Brain generating), thinking-pool AS (`ThinkingHandToChin`, `Thinking_01`/`_02`, DeepBreath, Remembering; Coy and ScratchingHead rarely) until he speaks. Never play Idle* overlays (`IdleLookingToSea_*`, `IdleStanding`, `IdleWeightShift`, `IdleRockingOnFeet`, SeaIdle exhibition hold) as the conversation hold.
- **First dialog hold (R15):** SeaIdle → dialog once uses `DialogGreetingPool` (`GreetingNod` / `SmallSmile` / `HaveASeat` / `Welcome`); then R9 listening deck.
- **In-dialog idle sequencing (R9):** play pool AS as one-shots in a shuffled non-repeating deck; blend AS→AS (do not section-loop one clip).
- **Speaking body (R14):** Brain plans distinct `[gesture:]` takes to cover the whole spoken line and must not repeat a CatalogId. Unreal plays each Brain take **once, to completion**; later markers that arrive while a take is still playing are queued, not used to cut it short. If Brain omitted a cue or the take ends while he is still talking, Unreal fills with a **different** basic explaining clip — never Greeting/Thinking/Idle, never a loop of the last stem. Conversation AS overlay **UpperBody** (spine_01+) over a planted `IdleStanding` DefaultSlot hold (R20). Presence Welcome / Greeting must not survive into (or after) speech. `[amused]` / `[emphasis]` / `[serious]` are mood only and must not leave Speaking or jump to Listening* while ACE is still playing.
- **Speak→listen (R16):** after audio/lipsync ends, keep speaking body ~1s, then long soft blend into Listening*. Do not start this hold from a mood cue.
- **Out of dialog (R13):** SeaIdle exhibition hold uses a shuffled calm-idle deck (`IdleLookingToSea_*`, standing/weight-shift/rocking, hands behind back) as soft-blended one-shots. Never section-loop a single SeaIdle AS. Do not use `HandsClasped` (drives hands/sleeves through the jacket; R23).
- **Speaking end:** Speaking body AS must end when audible ACE playback ends (audio-end watchdog from `OnAnimationStarted`), not only when HTTP `FinishStream` completes.
- **Idle re-engagement (R10):** after visitor inactivity, engagement prompts are owned by **Unreal**, not Brain timers/web idle nudge. Brain must not speak unsolicited to re-engage. Do not fire a quiet nudge if visitor speech is already detected; abort an in-flight nudge on `speech_started`. After two unanswered engagement prompts, assume they left, return to SeaIdle, then recapture the empty-room webcam baseline after 2s (waiting for the next visitor).
- **Visitor goodbye (R12):** Brain flags `conversationEnd` (and may emit a `[farewell]` cue); Unreal latches it via `RequestConversationEnd` and stays **in dialog** until the goodbye reply has finished speaking, then runs `BeginFarewell` from `NotifyUtteranceEnded`. Never start the farewell straight from the cue. After the wave, wait 3s for them to leave; if the room is still occupied (or someone speaks), arrival card then Welcome as a new visit.
